{"uid":"lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py","name":"csrf_flow.py","qualname":"lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py","kind":"module","file":"lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py","line":1,"end_line":204,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"End-to-end CSRF token flow for the LazyOwn C2 web layer.","description":"Contract: this module wires :class:`lazyc2.security.csrf.CSRFPolicy` into a\nFlask application so every authenticated browser session receives a token\nand every mutating request must echo it back. Non-browser clients (the CLI\ndriving the C2 over HTTP Basic) are exempt because a cross-site page cannot\nattach the operator's Basic credentials.\n\nFlow:\n\n1. ``before_request`` primes a stable per-session key inside the signed\n   Flask session and issues (or reuses) the token bound to that key.\n2. ``after_request`` attaches two cookies: the policy cookie (session key,\n   read back server-side by the gate, ``HttpOnly``) and a readable token\n   cookie the browser JavaScript echoes as the policy header. Both carry\n   ``Secure`` whenever ``secure_fn()`` reports TLS (or the request itself\n   arrived over HTTPS), and ``SameSite=Strict`` always.\n3. A context processor exposes the token to templates for hidden form\n   fields (``<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"xsrf_token\" value=\"{{ csrf_token }}\">``).\n\nThe pure token policy stays in :mod:`lazyc2.security.csrf`; only Flask\nwiring lives here.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py::SESSION_KEY","lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py::ensure_session_key","lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py::request_session_id","lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py::make_csrf_protect","lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py::register_csrf_flow","lazyc2/security/csrf_flow.py::token_cookie_name"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
